# THE TWO STEPS THAT LEAVE THE GRAPH — rendering the app, and running it.
#
# Everything else `pystrider` does happens inside a graph we own. These two do not, and that is why they are
# in their own file: `dispatch` is the one place an effect crosses the boundary, and `loop.verb_of` reads
# the instruction a task is ON to say — **before the step is taken** — whether it is a `look` or an `act`.
# A generator that could not make that distinction about its own output would be trusting a claim it had
# no way to state.
#
# ⭐⭐ **THE TWO ARE REGISTERED DIFFERENTLY AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT.** `render_app` is registered
# `observes=True`: it reads the graph and returns text, and nothing outside the machine can tell it ran.
# `drive_app` is registered without it, so it counts as changing the world — because it does: it `exec`s
# the source we just wrote and drives a real Textual app. A driver that declines irreversible steps takes
# the first and stops before the second, which is the last moment at which the whole generation could
# still be thrown away for free.
#
# ⚠ These are operations by category (`pystrider/library.py`) and the planner still cannot propose one:
# neither declares a return type, so `function.producers` never offers it. The safety property is NOT
# that we remembered to keep them out of the plan — it is that nothing can want them.
#
# ⚠ **THEY POLL, AND THE COORDINATION IS DATA ON THE BUILD NODE.** Both are scheduled at the start,
# before there is anything to render or run, because the alternative — Python scheduling each task at the
# moment it becomes possible — would put the pipeline's control flow back in Python, which is the thing
# the outer loop exists to end. So each waits for the state that makes it applicable, and the failure
# path is an authored flag (`abandoned`) rather than a Python `if`.

# Render the emitted app once the plan has been carried out — a LOOK, and it never runs anything.
fn render_the_app(b, p):
    .wait:
    ATTR R(phase) F(p) "phase"
    CONST R(finished) "done"
    EQ R(over) R(phase) R(finished)
    JMPNOT R(over) ".wait"
    ATTR R(ok) F(b) "finishes"
    JMPNOT R(ok) ".nothing"
    DISPATCH R(result) "render_app" F(b)
    JMP ".end"
    .nothing:
    SET F(b) "abandoned" "the generation did not reach an app to render"
    .end:

# Run it. ⚠ THE IRREVERSIBLE STEP. Everything before this can be discarded at no cost; after it, code we
# wrote has executed. It gives up honestly when the generation was abandoned rather than spinning.
fn run_the_app(b):
    .wait:
    ATTR R(source) F(b) "source"
    JMPIF R(source) ".ready"
    ATTR R(gone) F(b) "abandoned"
    JMPNOT R(gone) ".wait"
    JMP ".end"
    .ready:
    DISPATCH R(result) "drive_app" F(b)
    .end:
